{
  "id": "COMPOUND:43011 - PROTEIN:5836",
  "verbalization": "Mangostenone D is implicated in the biological activity of HUVEC cells through a series of molecular pathways. The evidence suggests that Mangostenone D acts as a target for SNU-387, which in turn is a target of two different compounds: 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One and 6,7-Dimethoxy-2-Methyl-3,4-Dihydroisoquinolin-1-One. Both of these compounds are known to have targets in HUVEC cells, indicating a potential downstream effect of Mangostenone D on these pathways. The presence of multiple targets for SNU-387, along with the direct targeting of HUVEC by these compounds, suggests a complex network of interactions that may be involved in the biological response of HUVEC to Mangostenone D. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of SNU-387 as a central mediator in the relationship between Mangostenone D and HUVEC, emphasizing the role of this compound in modulating cellular processes.",
